;; Reviewed 2026-10-10 by the user (written by Claude, from design
;; section 16, the LIB$ manual's condition values and the guest runs).
;; Why this is right:
;; - The fault's own status, as VMS ended the image: %X4BC, which the
;;   message in .err names FLTDIV_F, severity 4 (fatal), with bit 28
;;   set, as the system's default handler sets it after printing the
;;   message, so that $EXIT does not print it again. Not one of poc's
;;   trap statuses (%X10000000 + 8n + 2), so it maps to no exit code.
%X100004BC
